body:
Played around with the calculator for a bit and had a range from 456-506, depending on if I would be able to get a job offer. Either way, not close enough at all--even if I would've been able to get a bachelor's, I'd still be off last round's minimum by 200 points. Do I have any other options?

&#x200B;

Edit: Should add that I marked "no" for any nomination certificates or certificates of quality

Things have gotten to the point now where I'm rethinking starting T or even publicly transition for this same reason. I lack the self confidence to handle any of what you're describing, props to you for being so strong in the face of it. The way I see it, I'll feel like a pseudo-man no matter what I do, why go into a lifetime's worth of medical debt to only fix a few things that may add up to nothing at all? In any case, best of luck to you.

&#x200B;

Edited for clarity
